„­bible_version£KJV¤book:§chapter¨sections•…¤book:§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses’„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙYMy brethren, be not many masters, knowing that we shall receive the greater condemnation.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙƒFor in many things we offend all. If any man offend not in word, the same is a perfect man, and able also to bridle the whole body.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book:§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses”„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeBehold, we put bits in the horses' mouths, that they may obey us; and we turn about their whole body.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ«Behold also the ships, which though they be so great, and are driven of fierce winds, yet are they turned about with a very small helm, whithersoever the governor listeth.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙtEven so the tongue is a little member, and boasteth great things. Behold, how great a matter a little fire kindleth!¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ¼And the tongue is a fire, a world of iniquity: so is the tongue among our members, that it defileth the whole body, and setteth on fire the course of nature; and it is set on fire of hell.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book:§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses–„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙ|For every kind of beasts, and of birds, and of serpents, and of things in the sea, is tamed, and hath been tamed of mankind:¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙLbut the tongue can no man tame; it is an unruly evil, full of deadly poison.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse	¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙpTherewith bless we God, even the Father; and therewith curse we men, which are made after the similitude of God.¦layout ªlast_verse	„¥verse
